    writingguide_sweep_eval_test.go:99:   [1] axis=form severity=substantive repair=reword
              quote: Slice 4 of the session-subsystem rebuild (20260730-093011-d-tac-k4q), the transport-vocabulary directive it implements against, the branch-precedence consolidation, and a read-side recovery of lost session endings are delivered in commits `2e961f00`, `7b4fee69`, `1fb24286`, `627ed373` and `a08266b4` on branch worktree-k4q-session-rebuild
              reasoning: The first sentence lists what was delivered as four things — slice 4, the transport-vocabulary directive, the branch-precedence consolidation, and the read-side recovery — but names five commit hashes including `7b4fee69`, the retention day-parsing fix detailed two sentences later. A reader relying on the opening sentence as the entry's summary would come away thinking only four things landed and would miss that a defect fix shipped in the same batch; the ref annotation for d-tac-k4q, by contrast, does list 'the retention fix' among its five items, showing the omission is inconsistent within the draft itself.
    writingguide_sweep_eval_test.go:99:   [2] axis=conflation severity=substantive repair=split
              quote: The truth is the opposite: 36 of the store's 58 sessions have a completed shell and 17 more an abandoned one — Christopher concludes nearly every dialogue — but the engine recorded each conclude only as the shell's own event, while the metadata-level record the collector reads was never written, its write site lost in the mid-July session-model rebuild.
              reasoning: This sentence and its surrounding paragraph don't describe the act performed (building the read-side decorator) — they assert a standalone factual claim about the world: how many of the store's real sessions were actually concluded, and why the engine failed to record it. Per the done kind's own rule, 'when something noticed in the doing stands on its own — a problem, a claim, an open question — it becomes its own entry pointing back at this one; the done keeps the mention, not the full story,' but here the full diagnosis, with its figures and root-cause narrative, is carried entirely inside this done rather than in a fact/insight entry it could point back to.
    writingguide_sweep_eval_test.go:99:   [3] axis=dilution severity=minor repair=cut
              quote: The store was not full of unended dialogues; it was full of endings the engine had failed to record.
              reasoning: This sentence restates, in punchier form, the conclusion the immediately preceding sentence already established (that the store's conclude events existed but went unrecorded rather than the store being full of unended dialogues). Removing it loses no information a reader needs, only rhetorical emphasis.
