              quote: The store was not full of unended dialogues; it was full of endings the engine had failed to record.
              reasoning: Paragraph 6 doesn't just record that commit a08266b4 was made — it carries a full, self-standing claim about how the world is ('36 of the store's 58 sessions have a completed shell and 17 more an abandoned one... The store was not full of unended dialogues; it was full of endings the engine had failed to record'), overturning s-tac-jkw's prior diagnosis. Per the done kind's own rule, a claim noticed in the doing that stands on its own belongs in its own entry with the done keeping only the mention and a pointer back. The draft already applies exactly this split elsewhere for a different in-flight discovery (the config-strictness gap became its own signal, s-tac-8ae, cited by pointer only) — which makes the failure to do the same for the store-completion-rate insight an inconsistency, not a judgment call. A future reader reasoning about session-completion health would want this claim as its own fact/insight superseding jkw, not buried in a code-delivery done.
